Library5=lightruntimepermissions
ManifestCode=~\n~'Minimum required Android version & target SDK~\n~'Support Android 2.3.0 & later (API level 9+)~\n~'~\n~'Target API level 33 (Android 13)~\n~'It's also the minimum compile SDK version for AndroidX~\n~'~\n~'Avoid targeting API level 36+ (Android 16+)~\n~'~\n~'Otherwise some manifest attributes get ignored,~\n~'here "android:maxAspectRatio" & "android:resizeableActivity"~\n~AddManifestText(<uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion="9" android:targetSdkVersion="33" />)~\n~~\n~'Dislose that our App actually features functionality~\n~'that makes use of Camera hardware, but tell Android~\n~'that the Camera hardware isn't required for running~\n~'this application (QR code scanning is optional)~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera"           android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.autofocus" android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.front"     android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.any"       android:required="false" />~\n~<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.camera.flash"     android:required="false" />)~\n~~\n~'Supported device screen sizes & densities (all of them)~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<supports-screens android:smallScreens="true"~\n~                  android:normalScreens="true"~\n~                  android:largeScreens="true"~\n~                  android:xlargeScreens="true"~\n~                  android:anyDensity="true" />)~\n~~\n~'Opening browser URLs via Intents now requires more~\n~'Manifest declarations on Android 11 and later (API level 30+)~\n~AddManifestText(~\n~<queries>~\n~    <intent>~\n~        <action   android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />~\n~        <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />~\n~        <data android:scheme="https" />~\n~        <data android:scheme="http" />~\n~    </intent>~\n~</queries>)~\n~~\n~'Permissions are automatically added by Basic4Android~\n~'because they are declared in the NewQRCodeReaderView library~\n~~\n~'----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- -----~\n~~\n~'Application identity~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:label, "$LABEL$")~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:icon,  "@drawable/icon")~\n~~\n~'Application theme~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:theme, "@style/AppTheme")~\n~~\n~'Always detach this App's Activities from the task stack of other Apps~\n~'We do this by clearing its task affinity (setting it to "")~\n~'~\n~'Cans be set for <activity /> or <application />~\n~'Setting it in application covers the entire App~\n~'~\n~'This is done for security reasons, so that other apps~\n~'cannot do 'task reparenting' (StrandHogg) attacks on it~\n~SetApplicationAttribute("android:taskAffinity", "")~\n~~\n~'Performance optimization for Camera preview (QR code scanning)~\n~'We just do it for the entire application because why not~\n~SetApplicationAttribute(android:hardwareAccelerated, "true")~\n~~\n~'This App doesn't support multi-window mode~\n~'~\n~'Tell Android that this App hasn't been optimized for multi-window mode,~\n~'since otherwise the layouts will just look wrong anyway~\n~'~\n~'This preference is ignored for Apps targeting API level 36 or higher (Android 16+)~\n~'We can set it in either <activity /> or <application />~\n~SetApplicationAttribute("android:resizeableActivity", "false")~\n~~\n~'----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- -----~\n~~\n~'Don't let Android persist this App's state across~\n~'device reboots and on shutdowns~\n~'~\n~'We don't want the user having a leftover of this app's~\n~'old Activity states after the device restarts~\n~'~\n~'Introduced in API level 21 (Android 5.0)~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:persistableMode", "persistNever")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:persistableMode", "persistNever")~\n~~\n~'We don't want to let one original Android user launch this App's Activities,~\n~'then have other Android users on the same device being able to see the~\n~'original user's Activity in any task history (for security reasons)~\n~'~\n~'Each Android user account on a device should launch their own Activity if~\n~'they want to see it in their task histories~\n~'~\n~'Introduced in API level 23 (Android 6)~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:showForAllUsers", "false")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:showForAllUsers", "false")~\n~~\n~'Make the Main Activity exported (public)~\n~'~\n~'Android 12+ (API level 32+) requires that Activities~\n~'with <intent-filters /> must explicitly be marked as~\n~'exported Activities, for security reasons~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:exported", "true")~\n~~\n~'Make the QR scanner Activity non-exported (private)~\n~'It should only be callable by this app, not other ones~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:exported", "false")~\n~~\n~'Exclude the QR scanner Activity from the Recent Apps panel~\n~'Only the Main Activity should be visible in the Recent Apps list~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:excludeFromRecents", "true")~\n~~\n~'Turns out there's an Activity attribute for automatically~\n~'hiding the App's Activities from the Recent Apps panel~\n~'when they are closed (Activity finish)~\n~'~\n~'They only stay visible in the Recent Apps panel~\n~'as long as the user doesn't exit the App~\n~'~\n~'Introduced starting with API level 21 (Android 5.0)~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:autoRemoveFromRecents", "true")~\n~' - The Scan Activity is already excluded from the Recent Apps panel~\n~~\n~'Already set to singleTop by default by Basic4Android,~\n~'but we explicitly set it to singleTop anyway~\n~'~\n~'Atleast a singleTop or singleTask (worse one) launch mode~\n~'is required to receive onNewIntent Activity callbacks~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:launchMode", "singleTop")~\n~' - The Scan Activity doesn't need to receive Intents~\n~~\n~'Enforce stricter Intent matching rules for sharing~\n~'Intents to this app, by requiring that:~\n~' - Explicit Intents must match this app's component name~\n~' - Intents without any ACTION type don't match this app~\n~'~\n~'Set it for Activities that can receive Intents in this App~\n~'~\n~'Introduced in API level 36 (Android 16)~\n~'This attribute is also available for the <application /> field~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:intentMatchingFlags", "enforceIntentFilter")~\n~' - The Scan Activity doesn't receive Intents~\n~~\n~'Add a Share To functionality for receiving Admin key texts~\n~'~\n~'This allows other Android applications to send text to this App,~\n~'and if they are valid Hex strings they get used as Admin key input~\n~'~\n~'For example, you can generate an Hash in another App and forward~\n~'the generated hash to Android PIN Unblocker~\n~'~\n~' - "android:autoVerify"~\n~'   Introduced in API level 23 (Android 6)~\n~'~\n~'   It's some useless thing that's used for verifying~\n~'   Digital Asset Links JSON files on remote websites~\n~'~\n~' - "android:order":~\n~'   Introduced in API level 28 (Android 9)~\n~'~\n~'   This is the priority order of an Intent filter~\n~'   The higher the number, the higher the priority~\n~'~\n~'   It only manages the priority order of this App's own~\n~'   Intent filters, I don't want to use the "android:priority"~\n~'   Intent filter attribute since it would interfere with~\n~'   other apps' Intent filter offers,~\n~'   by taking priority over their own offers when you want to~\n~'   share text to a different application than this one~\n~'~\n~'   So out of courtesy for other apps, we only use~\n~'   the "android:order" Intent filter attribute~\n~AddActivityText(Main,~\n~<intent-filter android:label="Share Admin Key"~\n~               android:autoVerify="false"~\n~               android:order="1">~\n~	<action   android:name="android.intent.action.SEND" />~\n~	<category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />~\n~	<data     android:mimeType="text/plain" />~\n~</intent-filter>)~\n~~\n~'We don't care about Picture-in-Picture display mode~\n~'and we don't want to support it for security reasons~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:supportsPictureInPicture", "false")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:supportsPictureInPicture", "false")~\n~~\n~'Ask the connected display not to perform too much graphical~\n~'post-processing for this app (minimal post-processing)~\n~'~\n~'Some new-technology displays might try to improve the graphics,~\n~'colors, etc of an App but we don't need any such graphical enhancements~\n~'~\n~'Introduced in API level 30 (Android 11)~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:preferMinimalPostProcessing", "true")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:preferMinimalPostProcessing", "true")~\n~~\n~'Opt-out of predictive animations because we don't use~\n~'any animations in this app for performance reasons~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback", "false")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback", "false")~\n~~\n~'The maximum display aspect ratio that this app is~\n~'optimized for and supports is 16:9 (1.77)~\n~'~\n~'If the device has a much higher aspect ratio then~\n~'tell Android to letterbox the Activity View~\n~'~\n~'Letterboxing means scaling the Activity view while~\n~'preserving a 16:9 aspect ratio in this case~\n~'~\n~'Note: using a target SDK version of 36 or higher~\n~'      causes Android to ignore this attribute~\n~'~\n~' - API level 36 is Android 16~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:maxAspectRatio", "1.77")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:maxAspectRatio", "1.77")~\n~~\n~'Intercept mundane device configuration change events to~\n~'deliberately ignore them when they come to this app~\n~'~\n~'More info:~\n~' - https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/activity-element?hl=en#config~\n~' - https://stackoverflow.com/questions/9566633/how-to-use-onconfigurationchanged-and-newconfig-orientation-configuration-o~\n~'~\n~'Tell Android that we're going to handle these configuration change events~\n~'but we will actually simply ignore them, so that Android doesn't destroy~\n~'then recreate this app's Activities for mundane device configuration changes~\n~'that are not even related to the device display or its orientation~\n~'~\n~'For example, device orientation events are:~\n~' - orientation~\n~' - screenSize~\n~' - smallestScreenSize~\n~'~\n~'So we will hook all the other (useless) ones to ignore them~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Main, "android:configChanges", "colorMode|grammaticalGender|keyboard|keyboardHidden|locale|mcc|mnc|navigation|touchscreen")~\n~SetActivityAttribute(Scan, "android:configChanges", "colorMode|grammaticalGender|keyboard|keyboardHidden|locale|mcc|mnc|navigation|touchscreen")~\n~~\n~'----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- -----~\n~~\n~'~\n~'This part is for creating the application's resources~\n~'Also harden EditText fields with XML attributes when possible~\n~'~\n~~\n~'Android 8.0+ -> DeviceDefault parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values-v26, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV26" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV26" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV26</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowActivityTransitions">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV26" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV23">~\n~		<item name="android:imeOptions">flagNoExtractUi|flagNoFullscreen|flagNoPersonalizedLearning</item>~\n~		<item name="android:importantForAutofill">noExcludeDescendants</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 6-7.1~\n~CreateResource(values-v23, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV23" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV23" parent="@style/MyThemeV21">~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV23</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV23" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV11">~\n~		<item name="android:allowUndo">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 5.0-5.1.1 -> Material parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values-v21, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV21" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV21" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV11</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowActivityTransitions">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 3.0-4.4.4 -> Holo parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values-v11, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV11" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV11" parent="@android:style/Theme.Holo">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV11</item>~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV11" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV5">~\n~		<item name="android:imeOptions">flagNoExtractUi|flagNoFullscreen</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 2.3.3-2.3.7~\n~CreateResource(values-v10, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV10" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV10" parent="@style/MyThemeV5">~\n~		<item name="android:windowShowWallpaper">false</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 2.0-2.3.2~\n~CreateResource(values-v5, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV5" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV5" parent="@style/MyThemeV3">~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV5</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV5" parent="@style/MyEditTextStyleV3">~\n~		<item name="android:inputType">textVisiblePassword|textNoSuggestions</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 1.5-1.6~\n~CreateResource(values-v3, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyThemeV3" />~\n~	<style name="MyThemeV3" parent="@style/MyTheme">~\n~		<item name="android:editTextStyle">@style/MyEditTextStyleV3</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~	<style name="MyEditTextStyleV3" parent="@android:style/Widget.EditText">~\n~		<item name="android:inputType">textVisiblePassword</item>~\n~		<item name="android:imeOptions">flagNoExtractUi</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'Android 1.0-1.1 -> Theme parent theme~\n~CreateResource(values, styles.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<style name="AppTheme" parent="@style/MyTheme" />~\n~	<style name="MyTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme">~\n~		<item name="android:windowBackground">@color/MyWindowBackground</item>~\n~	</style>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'~\n~'Default Activity & application colors~\n~'~\n~~\n~'Android version doesn't matter (generic)~\n~'All versions need to pick the same color~\n~CreateResource(values, colors.xml,~\n~<resources>~\n~	<color name="MyWindowBackground">#1C1C1C</color>~\n~</resources>)~\n~~\n~'----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- ----- -----~\n~~\n~'This App doesn't have any background Service so we remove~\n~'the automatically added permission from the Manifest file~\n~'~\n~'This is always done as the last Manifest Editor action~\n~RemovePermission(android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE)~\n~~\n~~\n~
Module1=MyAdvanced
Module2=MyCommon
Module3=MyConstants
Module4=MyCryptography
Module5=MyForegroundRotationDetection
Module6=MySecurity
Module7=Scan
NumberOfFiles=3
NumberOfLibraries=5
NumberOfModules=7
Version=12.5
@EndOfDesignText@

#Region Project Attributes
	#ApplicationLabel: Android PIN Unblocker
	#VersionCode: 69
	#VersionName: 4.15.0
	
	#SupportedOrientations: unspecified
	#CanInstallToExternalStorage: False
	
	#If LOGGING
	#BridgeLogger: True
	#Else
	#BridgeLogger: False
	#End If
	#MultiDex:     False
	
	'For signing the app
	'You can also use your own keystore
	'
	'The key password is also used for opening the keystore file as well
	'Make sure both passwords are the same when using your own keystore
	'
	'The 'Working Directory' of all project options and custom build actions
	'is always the "Objects" folder, just so you know about it
	#SignKeyFile:      "..\Keystore\debug.keystore"
	#SignKeyAlgorithm: -digestalg SHA1 -sigalg SHA256withRSA
	#SignKeyAlias:     androiddebugkey
	#SignKeyPassword:  android
	
#End Region

#Region Activity Attributes
	#FullScreen:   False
	#IncludeTitle: True
	
#End Region

#Region Module File Attributes
	'Ignore "The recommended value for android:targetSdkVersion is x (manifest editor)" warning (#31)
	#IgnoreWarnings: 31
	
#End Region

#Region Project Macros
	'
	'Replace the full icon fonts with trimmed ones
	'
	'These specific fonts are also now required for
	'unofficial custom glyph additions, such as the
	'copyleft glyph (but also any future ones)
	'
	'More info:
	' - https://www.b4x.com/android/forum/threads/b4x-custombuildaction.168654/
	'
	'The default working directory is the "Objects" folder
	'
	'Robocopy switches:
	' - /MT: multi-threaded copy mode
	' - /E:  include (copy) subfolders and also the empty ones
	' - /IT: include (replace) tweaked files (not same file attributes)
	' - /IS: include (replace) same files
	#CustomBuildAction: folders ready, %WINDIR%\System32\robocopy.exe, "..\Fonts" ".\bin\extra\assets" /MT /E /IT /IS
	
#End Region

